Code review: Python class w/ Telnet interface to memcached
Critique: The pattern self.client.write("some command\n") response = self.client.read_until('END') appears three times in the code and should be refactored into its own method. In key_details, list comprehensions should be used instead of building up a list imperatively. Lastly, the if-else statement should be written using an else for optically pleasing code.

REVISED: 
import re, telnetlib

class MemcachedStats:

    _client = None

    def __init__(self, host='localhost', port='11211'):
        self._host = host
        self._port = port

    @property
    def client(self):
        if self._client is None:
            self._client = telnetlib.Telnet(self._host, self._port)
        return self._client

    def command(self, cmd):
        self.client.write("%s\n" % cmd)
        return self.client.r

