Code review: caching decorator
Critique: What you are trying to achieve is called memoization and has already a number of recipe available on the Python wiki. Your implementation matches the one using nested functions, but a few things to note here on top of yours are the usage of a local variable which resolves faster than an attribute lookup, the usage of functools.wraps which keeps some properties of the original function intact (name and docstring, mainly), and explicit names for variables.

