Code review: Compute power set of a given set in Python
Critique: Find the appropriate datatype for your problem. The power set is by definition a set. Redundant naming: It is obvious, that set() is an empty set. Don't abbreviate if it is not necessary. Names: Naming stuff is the hardest part. But I would call a power_set_item simply a subset. Operators: Use | instead of the union method. Copy: In general the best way to copy is to call the copy method. List Comprehension: Use list comprehensions to get rid of the new_sets variable. Datatype: Change the code to return a set of frozensets.

